        "title": "Bird Song and Communication",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Bird song is a model system for studying vocal learning, sexual selection, neural plasticity, and cultural evolution. The parallels with human language learning — critical periods, template-matching, cultural transmission — made avian song one of the most productive model systems in neuroscience. The vocal learning system has evolved independently in songbirds, parrots, and hummingbirds (the three avian vocal learners), with convergent brain circuitry."
